---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import prompt from '../../docs/RESEARCH_SESSION_PROTOCOL_PROMPT.md?raw';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
---
<Layout title="Memory Palace Protocol" description="The Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol v0.3 plus companion protocols for possibility management and low-friction epistemic artefact intake.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research operating protocol · Memory Palace v0.3 + Frontier companion v0.1 + Intake companion v0.1</p>
      <h1>A memory palace for the research process, with an exit from the palace.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The Memory Palace preserves how research emerged. Epistemic Intake catches materially distinct artefacts before judgment. The companion Possibility Portfolio prevents preservation from turning every branch into an obligation by separating the abundant option set from a deliberately small Active Frontier.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={internal('downloads/Agalmic_Research_Memory_Palace_Protocol_v0.3.md')} download>Download Memory Palace v0.3</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/POSSIBILITY_CAPTURE_AND_FRONTIER_PROMPT.md">Frontier companion prompt ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Standards correction</p>
        <h2>Provenance was already a field before we drew our graph.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The protocol treats the Memory Palace as an application profile and experimental extension.</p>
        <p>Use <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-dm/">W3C PROV</a> for ordinary provenance, <a href="https://credit.niso.org/">CRediT</a> for standardized scholarly contribution roles and <a href="https://www.researchobject.org/ro-crate/specification/1.3/">RO-Crate</a> for packaging research objects. Local fields are justified only where those systems do not adequately express the research question.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/STANDARDS_PROVENANCE_PROFILE.md">Read the standards-first profile ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Possibility preservation</p>
        <h2>The graph may be abundant. Commitment should not be.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">A research branch can remain valuable without becoming an active project.</p>
        <p>The companion protocol records a new idea as a possibility option with provenance, publication sensitivity, lineage status, the worthwhile future it could make more reachable, the capacity it could create and the cheapest discriminating next action.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Capture promiscuously. Commit selectively. Realize deliberately.</strong></p></div>
        <p>The Active Frontier defaults to no more than three substantial bets. A new candidate must take an available slot or explicitly displace an incumbent rather than silently adding another obligation.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('frontier')}>Inspect the Active Frontier</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/POSSIBILITY_PORTFOLIO_AND_ACTIVE_FRONTIER.md">Operating method ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Epistemic intake</p>
        <h2>Give new artefacts a room before asking what they are.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">Capture can be immediate even when judgment cannot.</p>
        <p>The Epistemic Intake Room records materially distinct research artefacts with provenance while allowing warrant, understanding, novelty and commitment to remain unresolved. Entry is deliberately cheap and does not promote an artefact to knowledge or active work.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Capture first. Judge deliberately. Promote sparingly.</strong></p></div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('intake')}>Enter Epistemic Intake</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/EPISTEMIC_ARTEFACT_INTAKE.md">Intake protocol ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Novelty discipline</p>
        <h2>The protocol searches the ancestors of an idea before celebrating its birth.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Novelty is a conclusion of search, not a tone of voice.</strong></p></div>
        <p>Every potentially publishable contribution must be classified against prior knowledge: established antecedent, independent rediscovery, synthesis, extension, application, operationalization, terminology candidate, novelty unassessed or candidate novelty. Exact-phrase novelty is not enough.</p>
        <p>The portfolio review also found that <strong>effective adjacent possible</strong> is already an explicit construct in Taalbi's innovation research, and that idea capture, portfolio selection and staged commitment all have mature antecedents.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('lineage')}>Inspect the living lineage register →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Discovery attribution</p>
        <h2>Record the acts before deciding who discovered.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The protocol distinguishes <strong>problem framing, candidate generation, significance recognition, validation, integration with prior knowledge and realization</strong>. Those events can belong to different humans, models, experts or institutions.</p>
        <p>W3C PROV can record the process without deciding the philosophical question of whether a current AI system is itself a knower or discoverer.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Novelty is a relation between a result and prior knowledge. Discovery attribution is a relation between a discovery episode and its contributors.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Combined short activation</p>
        <h2>Use this for ordinary Agalmic Research sessions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <blockquote class="activation">Activate the Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol v0.3 and the Possibility Portfolio protocol v0.1. Treat this session as a versioned graph of discovery. Use W3C PROV, RO-Crate and CRediT where applicable, extending them only for genuinely missing epistemic fields. Track contribution provenance separately from epistemic authority; search intellectual lineage before claiming novelty; preserve explored, rejected, deferred and surfaced-but-unexamined branches; and capture materially new ideas as options rather than obligations. For each serious possibility, record what worthwhile future it could make more reachable, what capacity it creates and the cheapest discriminating next action. Keep no more than three substantial Active Frontier commitments unless an explicit exception is justified. At closeout produce the Memory Palace Packet, standards-compatible provenance outputs and a Possibility Portfolio Patch. Do not infer expertise, novelty or attribution without evidence, and do not request or fabricate hidden chain-of-thought.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Canonical Memory Palace prompt</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>The complete v0.3 base protocol.</h2>
          <p>This page renders the repository source directly. The possibility/frontier method and epistemic intake are maintained as companions so they can evolve without silently rewriting the provenance protocol.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="protocol-text">{prompt}</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Related infrastructure</p>
        <h2>Preserve the process, then choose what deserves another move.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A provenance-complete session should aim to emit a human-readable Memory Palace Packet, PROV-O-aligned JSON-LD, contribution mappings, RO-Crate-compatible metadata and the small local extension needed for epistemic fields. Epistemic Intake catches material artefacts early; the companion portfolio then decides which resulting branches stay as options, enter handoff, become active, are realized, parked or retired.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('provenance')}>Explore provenance</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('frontier')}>Active Frontier</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .protocol-text {
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule, #c9c4b8);
      padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 2rem);
      font: 0.9rem/1.55 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.28);
      max-width: 100%;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .activation {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1rem;
      border-left: 3px solid currentColor;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>